---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---
<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy"
  updated={site.legal.updated}
  meta={`Applies to · ${site.storeName} for iOS`}
  description="Harvest Loop keeps your game progress on your device. No account, no ads, no data selling — only anonymous diagnostics and optional Game Center."
>
  <div class="legal__panel">
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <ul class="legal__checks">
      <li>Your game progress, settings, and tutorial state stay on your device.</li>
      <li>No account is required — we do not collect your name, email, or profile.</li>
      <li>We collect anonymous, aggregated usage and crash data to improve the game.</li>
      <li>No ads, no ad SDKs, no selling or sharing of your personal data. Ever.</li>
      <li>Game Center and in-app purchases are handled entirely by Apple.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>1 · Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    {site.studioLegal} is the data controller for the limited data described here. Contact:
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2 · What stays on your device</h2>
  <p>
    Everything you create while playing — saved runs, level progress within a run, sound and music
    preferences, tutorial completion state, and high-score records stored locally — is written to your
    device's local storage. This data is not uploaded to any Harvest Loop server, because we do not
    operate a server for user game content.
  </p>

  <h2>3 · No account required</h2>
  <p>
    Harvest Loop does not require you to create an account, sign in, or provide an email address to play.
    We do not collect contact information through the game unless you voluntarily email us for support.
  </p>

  <h2>4 · In-app purchases</h2>
  <p>
    Optional purchases (full game unlock and consumable hearts) are processed entirely by the Apple App Store.
    We use RevenueCat solely to validate purchase receipts and unlock content you have bought. We never receive
    your payment card, billing address, or full Apple account details — only the receipt token needed to confirm
    your purchase and let you restore it on a new device.
  </p>
  <ul class="legal__items">
    <li><strong>full_game</strong> — one-time non-consumable purchase that unlocks endless runs past the free level limit.</li>
    <li><strong>lives_3</strong> — consumable purchase that refills hearts after game over.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5 · Game Center</h2>
  <p>
    If you choose to sign in to Game Center, your high scores may be submitted to Apple's Game Center
    leaderboard ({site.bundleId}.highscore). Game Center is optional and managed entirely by Apple under
    Apple's privacy policy. We do not control Apple's handling of your Game Center profile.
  </p>

  <h2>6 · What we collect</h2>
  <p>To keep the game working and improve it, we may collect anonymous, aggregated diagnostics that are not linked to your identity:</p>
  <ul class="legal__items">
    <li><strong>Crash and error reports</strong> — device model, iOS version, app version, and technical stack traces.</li>
    <li><strong>Gameplay event counters</strong> — for example "a level was completed" or "a block was added", as counts only. Never personal information or free-text input.</li>
    <li><strong>Purchase validation tokens</strong> — receipt data from Apple needed to confirm purchases.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not collect your name, email, phone number, contacts, precise location, or advertising identifiers.
    We do not attempt to re-identify anonymous data. There is no free-text input in core gameplay.
  </p>

  <h2>7 · Children and families</h2>
  <p>
    Harvest Loop is designed as a family-friendly puzzle game. We do not knowingly collect personal information
    from children. The game contains no behavioral advertising, no third-party ad networks, and no social features
    that expose personal data. Parents can contact us at {site.email} with any questions.
  </p>

  <h2>8 · Service providers</h2>
  <p>We use a small number of processors strictly for the purposes above:</p>
  <ul class="legal__items">
    <li><strong>Apple</strong> — app distribution, in-app purchases, and Game Center.</li>
    <li><strong>RevenueCat</strong> — purchase receipt validation and entitlement management.</li>
    <li><strong>Analytics / crash reporting providers</strong> — anonymous diagnostics only, if enabled.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>9 · Data retention and deletion</h2>
  <p>
    Local game data remains on your device until you delete the app or clear its storage. Anonymous analytics
    data is retained only as long as needed for product improvement. To remove local data, delete Harvest Loop
    from your device. To request deletion of any data we may hold, email {site.email}.
  </p>

  <h2>10 · Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on your location, you may have rights to access, correct, or delete personal data we hold.
    Because we collect minimal data and no account is required, most requests can be fulfilled by deleting
    the app. Contact us at {site.email} for any privacy-related request.
  </p>

  <h2>11 · Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. The "Last updated" date at the top reflects the most recent
    revision. Continued use of the app after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
  </p>

  <div class="legal__contact">
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about privacy? Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Legal>
